{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03672",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.25,
      "end_seconds": 4.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.93,
      "end_seconds": 10.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.32,
      "end_seconds": 19.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Well, I've been having being a bit constipated."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.19,
      "end_seconds": 23.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Shall I check your blood pressure and pulse?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.31,
      "end_seconds": 39.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "That's it, just a little longer..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.36,
      "end_seconds": 72.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.91,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 97 percent, temperature is 37.0 degrees, blood pressure 117 over 80. And heart rate 85. When was the first time you noticed it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.04,
      "end_seconds": 76.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "It's been like this since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.98,
      "end_seconds": 80.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.29,
      "end_seconds": 94.5,
      "duration_seconds": 12.21,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get poor appetite for two days as well. And I've been feeling off as well, for five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.14,
      "end_seconds": 116.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Have you had any urinary symptoms or vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.63,
      "end_seconds": 119.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.82,
      "end_seconds": 124.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Any high fever or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.07,
      "end_seconds": 131.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "I haven't had high fever or blood in the stool, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.09,
      "end_seconds": 135.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Has your heart given you any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.45,
      "end_seconds": 137.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.4,
      "end_seconds": 142.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "And your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.18,
      "end_seconds": 144.24,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "Skin's normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.27,
      "end_seconds": 148.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.35,
      "end_seconds": 154.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.37,
      "end_seconds": 156.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.19,
      "end_seconds": 160.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.88,
      "end_seconds": 165.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Are you on your own at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.44,
      "end_seconds": 170.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.83,
      "end_seconds": 178.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "Okay, do you have any chronic illnesses? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.74,
      "end_seconds": 187.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "I have high blood pressure. I've had heart failure for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.75,
      "end_seconds": 202.15,
      "duration_seconds": 10.4,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Okay, I can see heart failure in your file as well. What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.66,
      "end_seconds": 208.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.15,
      "end_seconds": 211.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.63,
      "end_seconds": 215.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No surgery, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.66,
      "end_seconds": 233.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.65,
      "end_seconds": 239.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.27,
      "text": "Diclofenac. I come out in... well, swelling of my lips."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.42,
      "end_seconds": 244.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.09,
      "end_seconds": 248.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.85,
      "end_seconds": 265.88,
      "duration_seconds": 9.03,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft but tender low on the right with mild guarding, and the temperature is only a little up."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.59,
      "end_seconds": 271.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.68,
      "end_seconds": 306.45,
      "duration_seconds": 25.77,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? The most likely explanation is possible appendicitis, which can look mild in older people. Constipation is also on my list. I'm sending you for blood tests because of abdominal pain. Let's book a CT scan of the abdomen to look into right iliac fossa tenderness. Even though you look fairly well, I'd like the surgeons to see you today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.72,
      "end_seconds": 328.23,
      "duration_seconds": 16.51,
      "text": "Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. Let's plan a check straight away. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 328.81,
      "end_seconds": 331.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}